    Compositional one-ply bound B=sum L1 with soundness chain L0<=L1<=B<=F
    
    Probe for docs/research-compositional-lookahead.md: horizon-r lookahead
    Lr, series-factor compositional bound B, amplification along series
    powers, the exact gap family W^t (global L1=3t+1 vs B=F=4t), the
    no-fixed-horizon negative result for Q=Merge(2,1)=(2,0,0), and the
    optional capped linear-extension polynomial-space prune (O(n^2(d+1))
    bits, no O(2^n) downset array; total posets and d=0 handled as edge
    cases). Bounded regression: chain holds on all n<=5 posets (0 failures,
    no strict B>L1 below n=10); prune exactly equivalent to L1>d in 1210
    checks. Tests run in <1s; no n>=15 computation, no Lean changes.

